  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Government security classifications policy",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Procure > Finalise and publish procurement pack",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN applies to central government departments, their executive agencies and non-departmental public bodies (collectively referred to as ‘in-scope organisations’). It is also relevant to other contracting authorities which create, process, store and manage government information.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations must ensure that appropriate protective security controls are in place for new and existing contracts in line with the updated Government Security Classifications Policy 2023 (GSCP).",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The GSCP sets out the administrative system used by HM Government (HMG) to protect information and data assets appropriately against prevalent threats through the use of ‘classification tiers’.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "HMG uses three classification tiers; OFFICIAL, SECRET and TOP SECRET. Each tier provides a set of recommended baseline behaviours and a set of protective controls, which are proportionate to the threat profile for that tier AND the potential impact of a compromise, accidental loss or incorrect disclosure of information held within that tier.",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Sensitive information for all new contracts must be handled in accordance with the appropriate security classifications and protections under the GSCP.",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations should:",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure the procurement and contract documents refer to the appropriate GSCP classifications and are clearly marked, where possible, with a classification tier.",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Legal framework",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The PPN should be read alongside the relevant parts of the legal framework, including but not limited to, the following provisions of the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (which may be particularly relevant to the consideration of this PPN):",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 15: Defence and security",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 21: Confidentiality",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "Government security classifications policy",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Regulation 22 (18) and (19): General principles about the use of electronic and non-electronic means of communication",
      "ordinal": 16,
